0.7.9:
[x] - The click-to-select tool keeps working after the app preview reloads, instead of going dead until you click it twice.
[x] - DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (Fireworks) is a new choice in the model dropdown — 1M context, reads images, and faster/cheaper than V4 Pro. Checked Muse Spark 1.3 the same day: still registered but our Meta account cannot reach it (404), so it stays greyed out.
[x] - On a ChatGPT/Codex-authenticated thread, Leo no longer shows you raw JSON before it asks its question.
[x] - You can rate a reply with 👍/👎 while Leo is still writing it, instead of waiting for the run to finish.
[x] - The pointer/select-element tool in the purple feedback bubble now works on phones and tablets: tap to highlight, tap Use this to confirm, and a banner with a Cancel button means you are never stuck in selection mode with no way out.
[x] - The screenshot annotator's arrow, box and text tools no longer refuse to draw on top of an annotation you already made — and drawing near an existing arrow no longer drags it across the image. A new Move tool repositions annotations when you actually want that.
[x] - Leo knows about the recipes you saved to your personal cookbook, so you can say "use the design system I saved from my other Leo" instead of picking it from the /cookbook menu every time.
[x] - The "2 JavaScript errors detected" notice still appears in a custom Leo mode, but it no longer ships the errors to that agent on its own — the Show Leo box starts unchecked there and stays checked in Beginner/Engineer/Ticket mode. A custom mode is somebody else's agent and may have no idea what to do with a stack trace; tick the box yourself when it does.
[x] - Turning the code editor on for the first time now sets up its `ssh leonardo` connection for you. Before, a brand-new editor had an empty SSH config and `ssh leonardo` failed with "Could not resolve hostname leonardo"; boxes already in that state repair themselves the next time the editor is toggled off and on.
[x] - Answering a question card Leo has already moved past now tells you so in the chat instead of killing the turn with a red "Error resuming after question: BadRequestError: 400 ... `messages` must contain at least one message with role `user` or `tool`". There was nothing left for the answer to resume, so the agent was being restarted with no conversation at all — which is the request the provider was rejecting.
[x] - Screenshots taken from the chat toolbar are now cropped to the app preview on the right, instead of including the chat panel beside it. In Chrome/Edge the browser crops the capture to the preview itself; elsewhere we crop the pixels ourselves when you share the tab, and fall back to the full shot (which you can still crop by hand) when you share a window or a whole screen.
[x] - Cancelling a feedback screenshot (Cancel on the drag screen, Cancel or × on the annotate screen, or a capture that fails) brings the feedback panel back with your draft still in it. Before, the panel stayed hidden and the only way back was a reload.
[x] - Security: the browser chat connection is now signed with a key unique to each box. Before, it used a key anyone could look up, so someone who knew it could open an engineer-mode chat on any box without an account. Nothing to configure — each box derives its key from its own private session secret; an operator-set WS_SECRET_KEY still takes priority.
[x] - Leo no longer "summarizes the conversation" after your first message. Reading one big file (like db/schema.rb) early in a new chat made Leo think the conversation was ~8x bigger than it was, so it compacted almost immediately and lost the file it had just read. Big files now also come back one page at a time (about 25,000 characters), with a note telling Leo where the next page starts.
